WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(lively music)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:04.320
(crowd applauds)

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.250
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.083
You look great.

00:00:06.083 --> 00:00:06.916
Congratulations.

00:00:06.916 --> 00:00:08.070
- Oh my gosh, thank you.
- You have a baby boy right?

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.209
- Baby boy, yes.

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:11.189
- [Kelly] Was it exciting?
(crowd applauds)

00:00:11.189 --> 00:00:12.330
That's exciting.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.550
I was excited when I found out

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.080
because I had a little girl just like you.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.070
And then I had a little boy,

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.650
and I was excited because I
got one of both, were you?

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.590
- I'm one of both, and I think I'm good.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:23.423
- [Kelly] You're done?

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.390
- Shop is closed, yes.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.100
One of each.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.120
It's exciting.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.810
It definitely was, you
know, just a different way,

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:31.920
I did surrogacy.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.720
- [Kelly] Yeah, this second time, right?

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:34.680
- The second time, yes.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.650
The first time I carried on my own.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.450
The second time I did surrogacy.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.430
And it's, I mean, it's amazing.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.890
- I wish I had known about that,
I had horrible pregnancies.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.450
I was like hospitalized, and so-

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:46.283
- Oh my gosh..

00:00:46.283 --> 00:00:48.300
- Yeah, but I didn't
really even know about it

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.900
or know what it was like in
my circle, but it's brilliant.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.040
- It's amazing.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.740
I had reasons why I
couldn't carry my second.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:56.573
- [Kelly] No, me too.

00:00:56.573 --> 00:00:57.406
- Right.

00:00:57.406 --> 00:00:59.760
- And it's such a blessing
that we have this.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.550
My sister Kim had two
babies through surrogacy,

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.170
she had two that she carried on her own

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.570
and her last two are through surrogacy.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.065
If it wasn't for Kimberly, I definitely

00:01:09.065 --> 00:01:10.260
don't think I would've
been as comfortable.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.100
- You wouldn't have been aware?

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.530
- I wouldn't have been aware,
I wouldn't have know as much.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:17.640
I watched her go through her
journey, and I'm so grateful

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.610
for how open she's always been
about her journey because...

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:21.840
And not every journey is the same,

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.360
mine was very different from hers.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:29.010
I think her journey was way more...

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.710
I think she was more, maybe not involved,

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:32.580
I don't know the term, but like,

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:33.990
it was just more comfortable for her.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.780
For me I'm such a control freak.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.400
- Oh yeah, you'd be like,
"What are they eating?

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.233
What are they drinking?

00:01:39.233 --> 00:01:40.066
What are they putting in their body?"

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.400
- You're a stranger, I
just have to trust you?

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.800
And I love my surrogate, she was amazing,

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.080
but I'm still like, I need
you sitting next to me

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:47.850
all the time, I need to
know what you're doing,

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.170
what are you eating?

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:50.820
So it was-

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.400
- [Kelly] I think I would've
been a little like that too

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:54.233
had I known, yeah.

00:01:54.233 --> 00:01:56.100
- And a control freak,
I take as a compliment,

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.466
So I'm not offended that
I'm a control freak.

00:01:57.466 --> 00:01:58.470
- I don't know if it's like a control...

00:01:58.470 --> 00:01:59.610
Because people always say control freak,

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.710
but it's like, or you just
know what you want in life.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:02.827
- You're very particular.

00:02:02.827 --> 00:02:04.650
- [Kelly] Yeah, I think that that's fine.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.330
- It's not fine for other people,

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:07.710
but it's great for me.
- It cuts through the BS.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.350
Yeah, I think they need
to just get over it.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:13.050
So wait, so you haven't
revealed your son's name yet,

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:16.350
so is it like a family name, like a hint?

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:19.560
- Well, my daughter
says his name is Snowy.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:20.393
- [Kelly] Oh, your daughter?

00:02:20.393 --> 00:02:22.200
- It's not Snowy, so that's the hint.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.510
- I was like, were you a
big Game of Thrones fan?

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:25.343
- Oh my god.

00:02:25.343 --> 00:02:26.176
- Jon Snow.

00:02:26.176 --> 00:02:29.340
- I swear she just does things
to sort of like mess with me.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.290
But his name is not Snowy

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.780
- Wait, was she excited,
because my daughter was...

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.040
I don't know how far apart yours are,

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.720
mine are like 22 months apart.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.870
- She's four and he's three months.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:41.490
- Oh, so she is like a little doll to him?

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:42.360
- [Khloé] Yes.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.070
So I think she's at the age where...

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:46.740
And Kylie, my sister, just had a baby

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:51.000
and so I think it was like,
it's like cool for her,

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.710
like "Oh I have a baby too."

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:55.350
So I think that's the fun part for her.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:56.760
But True is my girl,

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:57.984
so I think if it was just...

00:02:57.984 --> 00:02:59.154
(audience coos)

00:02:59.154 --> 00:03:00.630
- Oh my gosh.
- That's my little girl.

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:02.250
And it's her and I all the time,

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.010
so I think if, thank God Kylie had a baby,

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:08.550
because I think she
probably would've like,

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:09.383
suffocated him or something.

00:03:09.383 --> 00:03:10.770
- It's so funny, it goes both ways,

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:11.760
no, it goes both ways.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.147
They get very upset because they're like,

00:03:13.147 --> 00:03:15.480
"No, she's mine," like to Mommy.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:18.990
But like at the same time
she loves to play Mommy.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:19.823
- Yeah.

00:03:19.823 --> 00:03:21.030
- But True's going to school now.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:22.710
So how's that adjustment been?
- She goes to school.

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:24.210
- It's weird because they're
in the house all the time

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.050
and then they're gone.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.300
- School is really strange.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.220
I mean, I thought, okay, you go to school

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.780
and it's like half a day.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:31.613
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:31.613 --> 00:03:33.900
- No, at this school they go a full day.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.910
They're like real adults, I'm so sad.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:38.040
It's probably harder on
me than it is on her.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.170
But she knows how to work me.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.510
So like the first two
weeks were really hard,

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.580
it was tears for both of us every day.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.290
Like I just felt like a monster,

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.570
I'm leaving her there and she's crying,

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:49.440
like, I didn't know what to do,

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.870
so I would always be sitting
right outside the door

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.730
and waiting and the teacher's
like, "You need to leave.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:54.684
You're making this worse."

00:03:54.684 --> 00:03:55.517
(kelly laughs)

00:03:55.517 --> 00:03:57.570
And I'm like, I'm one of those moms now.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:01.170
But I know school's great,
I just think it's so weird,

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.630
I'm used to having her
with me all the time.

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:05.880
And also the whole like, I thought, oh,

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:09.510
you get like a break in the
day when your kid's at school.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:11.580
No, you're going to school,

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.370
you make the lunches, do the
snacks, you go to carpool,

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:16.620
I'm lingering at the
school for like two hours

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.330
because I'm like making sure she's good.

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:22.140
By the time I get home you have
like, what, a couple hours,

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.090
like one or two hours, and you
have to go all the way back

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:24.930
and do the whole thing again.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.090
I'm like, this is forever?

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:29.760
- I think maybe you're like
a better mom or something,

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.577
because my daughter was like, "Deuces,"

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.557
I was like listening to
her, my daughter was like,

00:04:35.557 --> 00:04:37.020
"Peace, I'm gonna be good,"

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.296
like she didn't even-

00:04:38.296 --> 00:04:39.300
- That would've been so much easier.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.720
- I mean, yes, but like, I
kind of was like, I guess,

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:46.320
okay, maybe this is our
way of our love language.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.280
- No, I think that means

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:49.140
you raised a really independent girl.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.610
- She's very independent

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:51.443
- And that's great.

00:04:51.443 --> 00:04:54.570
I think I've babied
True, like, I did this,

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:58.110
I created this monster, but
I'm sick and I sort of love it.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:58.943
- You know what though?

00:04:58.943 --> 00:05:00.390
I think what's different
though, is parents,

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:02.820
your generation too, like
with your generation of kid,

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.740
it's like, y'all were in COVID too

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:05.880
for a couple years with your kids,

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:07.020
and everybody was locked down, right?

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:08.550
So that's a different thing.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:11.010
She in those like developmental years,

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.480
she's like with you constantly,

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:13.950
I think that was different too.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:14.850
- And I love it.

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:15.861
I'm sick.

00:05:15.861 --> 00:05:16.694
(kelly laughs)

00:05:16.694 --> 00:05:19.775
I'm like, yes, you need me
and you don't wanna leave me.

00:05:19.775 --> 00:05:20.608
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:05:20.608 --> 00:05:21.441
- I'm sick.

00:05:21.441 --> 00:05:23.730
Like if she would've been like,
"Deuces," I would've sobbed

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:25.321
and gone to a therapist immediately.

00:05:25.321 --> 00:05:26.786
(crowd laughs)

00:05:26.786 --> 00:05:28.124
- And I did not.

00:05:28.124 --> 00:05:29.220
(khloé laughs)

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.414
- You're like, "Bye."

00:05:30.414 --> 00:05:31.740
- I was like, you know what,
you should get into dance,

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:33.060
you should get into chess.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.950
I was like, all the afterschool programs.

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:36.270
- How long do you wanna be here for?

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.940
- Yeah, I'm like, well, and
also there's so many cool,

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.530
I don't know like what kind
of school you grew up in,

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:41.760
but the school I grew up in didn't have as

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:43.260
many opportunities as they have now.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:45.150
And I'm just like, girl
you got all these things

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.370
you could be doing at this
school, that's so awesome.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:49.385
- And I get so excited that she can.

00:05:49.385 --> 00:05:52.710
They do baking and different
instrument stuff set.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:54.390
Like it's so exciting what they have,

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:55.260
I didn't have all that either.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.447
- [Kelly] I know.

00:05:56.447 --> 00:05:57.280
- But it is cool

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:58.170
- It's cool to volunteer
too, just to see your kids

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.084
like with other little humans existing.

00:06:00.084 --> 00:06:00.930
- [Khloé] I know, I'll never leave.

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:02.533
And you're like, all
right, I'm doing all right.

00:06:02.533 --> 00:06:03.366
- [Khloé] I know.

00:06:03.366 --> 00:06:05.070
- Or like, oh God, we
should all go to therapy.

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:07.020
So in that clip you are talking

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:08.730
about living next door to your mom.

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:10.403
So how is that?

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:12.480
Because I love my mom.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:13.410
I'm just saying, I don't even know

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.990
if my mom would wanna live
like right next door to me.

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.191
- I told you, we're sick.

00:06:17.191 --> 00:06:18.024
(crowd laughs)

00:06:18.024 --> 00:06:20.083
Like, we're weirdly
co-dependent on each other.

00:06:20.083 --> 00:06:21.644
- [Kelly] You're a unit, though.

00:06:21.644 --> 00:06:23.130
- We're a tribe, and we always say that.

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:26.580
And my mom and I live literally next door,

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.200
like we removed the property line,

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.540
and our house is like one big house.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.412
I mean we have our own homes.

00:06:32.412 --> 00:06:33.270
- It's like a compound kind of thing.

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:34.103
- Yeah, it's like a compound.

00:06:34.103 --> 00:06:36.510
And then my other siblings
live in the same gated area.

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:38.880
So we're all in the same gated area.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:42.570
And my mom is typically really cool

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:43.680
and chill and she's great.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:46.110
So she's not an annoying mom to live with.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:47.130
- Yeah, like a hoverer?

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.800
- Yeah, she's not a
helicopter mom, and she's fun,

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.860
but there are moments that I'm,
like, a little creeped out.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:56.353
Like, okay, like you're
definitely watching me.

00:06:56.353 --> 00:06:57.186
(kelly laughs)

00:06:57.186 --> 00:06:59.730
Like the other day she
called and she was like,

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:01.620
it must have been 6:30 in the morning,

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:05.010
And she's like, "Who
just left your house?"

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.980
And I said, "Oh my God,
Who? I have no idea."

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:09.300
I genuinely had no idea.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.430
And she's like, "I saw
white Porsche leaving,

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:12.960
tell me who slept over."

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:15.030
I go, "No, it's 6:30."

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.890
I'm thinking like, who was in my driveway?

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:19.267
And we called security and they were like

00:07:19.267 --> 00:07:20.970
"Oh that was your mom's"

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:22.890
It was someone from my mom's house.

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:25.650
But I was like, why are
you looking out the window

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:27.540
wondering what car is coming or going?

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:28.770
It's 6:30 in the morning,

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:30.751
how long have you been
perched there watching me?

00:07:30.751 --> 00:07:32.430
(kelly laughs)

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:33.425
Like the whole thing, it's a little weird.

00:07:33.425 --> 00:07:34.410
- Perched?

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:37.050
- So I don't know how often she does that.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:41.220
And also that was her own
car, or someone for her house.

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:42.053
So, I don't know why she's watching.

00:07:42.053 --> 00:07:44.110
- I love that it was
someone that works with her

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:44.943
- [Khloé] Yes.

00:07:44.943 --> 00:07:45.776
that was at your house.

00:07:45.776 --> 00:07:46.609
- That she didn't even know.

00:07:46.609 --> 00:07:47.520
I was like, "I don't know."

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:48.900
But it did freak me out a little bit.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.040
But then I got more freaked out,

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:53.010
I'm like, how often are you watching me?

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:54.510
- I love that, how open y'all are.

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:55.620
Even though that conversation though,

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:56.820
that's pretty cool.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:59.550
Anyway, you recently had a melanoma scare.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:00.720
I didn't know this, somebody said this.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:01.740
So are you okay now?

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:03.390
- Well, hence the tape on my face.

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:04.740
I thought, maybe.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:06.030
But what happened?

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:11.010
- So I am just predisposed
to skin cancer, I assume.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:14.040
I had melanoma removed
from my back when I was 19.

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:14.873
- [Kelly] Oh wow.

00:08:14.873 --> 00:08:18.720
- And the reason why I'm
wanting to talk about this,

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:21.783
well one it's on my face, and it's been,

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:25.170
I had an operation, I
wanna say, I don't know,

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:29.520
eight weeks ago, something
like that, and people just...

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:31.620
There were all these stories
and all these things,

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:34.320
and I just was like, you know
what, it's bringing awareness,

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:36.420
it's for a good cause
at the end of the day.

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:38.460
I really just wanna highlight people

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:41.160
making sure that they
do their regular checks.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:42.330
I go every three months

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.850
because I am at higher
risk for skin cancer.

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:46.620
But as you just saw on the screen,

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:49.260
it was the smallest little bump,

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:52.050
and for months I thought it
was just like a cystic pimple,

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:53.610
I got it shot with cortisone.

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:56.520
No one thought anything of
it, but it wouldn't go down.

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:59.850
And so I got it checked
and someone was like,

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:00.960
let's just biopsy it.

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.680
We shaved it, it came
back, and they were saying,

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:07.770
there's no way you at your
age, I'm 38, I guess melanoma's

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:11.130
like really more for either
really young kids or older,

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:13.200
I'm not a doctor so I'm not
gonna talk too much about this

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.460
in case I'm screwing anything up.

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:15.293
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:15.293 --> 00:09:18.180
- But we had to do a second
biopsy and it came back

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:20.430
that it was a tumor and
they had to operate.

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:22.920
And so I was like, "A tumor?" In my head,

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:25.350
tumors are like, these big
things that are hanging,

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.990
like, you know, what
you see in the movies.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:32.880
So it was never once, I
never thought it was a tumor.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.313
And so I'm really grateful
that I was proactive.

00:09:36.243 --> 00:09:38.310
And we did the surgery, we got it removed,

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:40.260
and now I'm just healing,
and I have a scar,

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:41.842
and that will figure out.

00:09:41.842 --> 00:09:43.170
- Like, I think a lot of us

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:45.160
are making dermatologists
appointments right now.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:46.800
Like, that's what I'm doing.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:48.480
- But that's what I'm so grateful for,

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:51.060
because I have had a couple
people that because of me

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:52.590
they've gone to their dermatologists,

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:54.150
they have had things, biopsies.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.590
I've had friends that have had things

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:57.450
precancerous that are now removed.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.460
And, you know, knowledge is power,

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:01.980
and if you know something you
can do something about it.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.303
- [Kelly] Oh, I wanna know
right off the bat, yeah.

00:10:03.303 --> 00:10:04.346
- Yes, I'm that way too.

00:10:04.346 --> 00:10:05.179
(audience applauds)

00:10:05.179 --> 00:10:06.810
- Yeah, I'm always,
like, getting checked up

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:08.157
with everything like that.

